+# Free-Text Veterinarian Search Stays Out; Filtering the Directory Comes In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. As written it declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian in a single line. That line drew no boundary between typing a name into a search box and narrowing a list the directory already prints.
+
+A request arrived on 2026-08-16 to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty. Read against the old row, the request could be taken either way. The owner decided the row rather than letting the request settle it by implication.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-9 whole.** Rejected: it would decline a capability the owner has asked for, on a rationale about free-text search that the request does not exercise.
+2. **Drop NG-9.** Rejected: it would open free-text search across pets, visits, and veterinarians, which the owner did not ask for and which the original rationale still covers.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian stays out of scope. Narrowing the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope. The specialty filter recorded as `REQ-VET-004` is the first capability the narrowing admits.
+
+The narrowing is bounded by what the directory already prints. An attribute the directory does not show is not admitted by this decision, and a future request touching NG-9 again proceeds only on a fresh recorded owner decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The veterinarian directory gains a specialty filter on both its published forms.
+- Owner search remains the only free-text search in the sample, so the paged prefix-search pattern is still demonstrated once.
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation. Every other undecided row remains part of it.
+- The filter is an address contract. Whether the directory gains a visible control is recorded as an open question, not settled here.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-004) — the capability the narrowing admits.
